  "beats": [
    {
      "beat": 1,
      "text": "Elias's newspaper was dated tomorrow.",
      "start": 0.25,
      "end": 2.723,
      "duration": 2.473
    },
    {
      "beat": 2,
      "text": "He lived alone. He had no subscription.",
      "start": 2.923,
      "end": 5.175,
      "duration": 2.252
    },
    {
      "beat": 3,
      "text": "A misprint — until page nine reported his death.",
      "start": 5.375,
      "end": 8.684,
      "duration": 3.309
    },
    {
      "beat": 4,
      "text": "Apartment fire. Friday. Three a.m. His name.",
      "start": 8.884,
      "end": 12.634,
      "duration": 3.75
    },
    {
      "beat": 5,
      "text": "He booked a hotel across town.",
      "start": 12.834,
      "end": 14.808,
      "duration": 1.974
    },
    {
      "beat": 6,
      "text": "Saturday's paper was at the front desk.",
      "start": 15.008,
      "end": 17.423,
      "duration": 2.415
    },
    {
      "beat": 7,
      "text": "The fire happened anyway. Same building. Same hour. Different man.",
      "start": 17.623,
      "end": 21.837,
      "duration": 4.214
    },
    {
      "beat": 8,
      "text": "The dead man was his neighbour, who'd knocked to warn him.",
      "start": 22.037,
      "end": 25.358,
      "duration": 3.321
    },
    {
      "beat": 9,
      "text": "Elias spread every paper he'd saved across the floor.",
      "start": 25.558,
      "end": 28.983,
      "duration": 3.425
    },
    {
      "beat": 10,
      "text": "All dated tomorrow. Each mentioned him less than the last.",
      "start": 29.183,
      "end": 32.77,
      "duration": 3.587
    },
    {
      "beat": 11,
      "text": "First his job. Then his friends. Then the crossword.",
      "start": 32.97,
      "end": 36.36,
      "duration": 3.39
    },
    {
      "beat": 12,
      "text": "By Friday, his photograph was a grey rectangle.",
      "start": 36.56,
      "end": 39.811,
      "duration": 3.251
    },
    {
      "beat": 13,
      "text": "Saturday's paper arrived blank. Only the masthead remained.",
      "start": 40.011,
      "end": 44.063,
      "duration": 4.052
    },
    {
      "beat": 14,
      "text": "The Midnight Archive: all the news that never was.",
      "start": 44.263,
      "end": 47.85,
      "duration": 3.587
    },
    {
      "beat": 15,
      "text": "Elias finally understood. It wasn't predicting his future.",
      "start": 48.05,
      "end": 52.16,
      "duration": 4.11
    },
    {
      "beat": 16,
      "text": "It was deciding what to keep.",
      "start": 52.36,
      "end": 53.893,
      "duration": 1.533
    }
  ],
